; The mirror of guarded-hypot: the sign-definite operand is negative, so the
; guard reduces to a negated variable and comes out as (> 0 x) with the arms the
; other way round.  Worth keeping as an example because the other two only ever
; exercise (> v 0).
(FPCore (x)
  :name "-sqrt(x*x+1) - x"
  :pre (<= -10 x 10)
  (- (- (sqrt (+ (* x x) 1))) x))
